## Included

- layered Clean Architecture;
- environment-based configuration;
- multi-stage Docker build running as non-root;
- deterministic regeneration through `.gosvc/manifest.json`;
- tests, coverage gate, golangci-lint, govulncheck and CI;
{{if eq .Preset.Name "bare"}}- application entrypoint without HTTP/database adapters;
{{else if eq .Preset.Name "worker"}}- long-running context-aware worker entrypoint without HTTP/database adapters;
{{else}}- {{.Config.API.Router}} HTTP router with timeouts and graceful shutdown;
- `/health/live` and `/health/ready`;
{{end}}{{if .Config.Database.Enabled}}- PostgreSQL and versioned migrations through `golang-migrate`;
{{if eq .Config.Database.CodeGeneration "sqlc"}}- pgx/pgxpool + type-safe SQL through `sqlc`;
{{else}}- GORM with the PostgreSQL driver and `database/sql` pool management;
{{end}}- Docker Compose with PostgreSQL;
- repository/transaction examples and CRUD resource generation;
{{end}}{{if .Config.OpenAPI.Enabled}}- OpenAPI-first contract, request validation and `oapi-codegen`;
- ReDoc at `/docs` and raw contract at `/openapi.yaml`;
{{end}}{{if or (eq .Preset.Name "production-api") (eq .Preset.Name "event-driven-api")}}- JWT access tokens, rotating refresh sessions, RBAC and rate limiting;
- slog, Prometheus, OpenTelemetry and private pprof;
{{end}}{{if eq .Preset.Name "event-driven-api"}}- Redis, Kafka, Transactional Outbox, DLQ, worker and Kubernetes manifests;
{{end}}
## First run

Normalize dependencies/generated artifacts first:

```bash
make bootstrap
```

Then validate the concrete project with the installed generator:

```bash
gosvc doctor --project .
```

{{if .Config.Database.Enabled}}Start PostgreSQL and migrate:

```bash
docker compose up -d postgres
export DATABASE_URL='postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/{{.Config.Project.Name}}?sslmode=disable'
make migrate-up
```

{{end}}{{if or (eq .Preset.Name "production-api") (eq .Preset.Name "event-driven-api")}}Set a strong development JWT secret before running:

```bash
export JWT_SECRET="$(openssl rand -base64 48)"
```

{{end}}Run the quality gates and start the service/process:

```bash
make verify
make run
```

{{if .Config.API.Enabled}}Health endpoints:

```text
GET /health/live
GET /health/ready
```
{{end}}
{{if or (eq .Preset.Name "production-api") (eq .Preset.Name "event-driven-api")}}## Create the first user

```bash
PASSWORD_HASH="$(go run ./cmd/hash-password 'change-this-password')"

docker compose exec -T postgres psql \
  -U postgres \
  -d {{.Config.Project.Name}} \
  -v password_hash="$PASSWORD_HASH" <<'SQL'
INSERT INTO users (id, email, password_hash, roles)
VALUES (
  '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
  'admin@example.com',
  :'password_hash',
  ARRAY['admin']
)
ON CONFLICT (email) DO NOTHING;
SQL
```

Do not reuse development credentials or secrets in production.

## Authentication

```bash
curl -i -c cookies.txt \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"email":"admin@example.com","password":"change-this-password"}' \
  http://localhost:{{.Config.API.Port}}/auth/login
```

Protected routes use `Authorization: Bearer <access-token>`. Refresh/logout use the HttpOnly refresh cookie.

{{end}}{{if eq .Preset.Name "event-driven-api"}}## Event-driven runtime

```bash
make run
make run-worker
```

The Outbox worker claims rows transactionally, publishes to Kafka, and routes exhausted attempts to the configured DLQ. Redis provides idempotency primitives.

