## Upgrade

```bash
gosvc upgrade --project . --dry-run
gosvc upgrade --project .
gosvc upgrade --project . --preset-version {{.Preset.Version}} --dry-run
```

Preset identity is versioned independently from the CLI in `project.preset_version`. Changing preset versions is an upgrade operation, not an implicit regeneration side effect.

## Plugins

```bash
gosvc plugins list --project .
gosvc plugins validate --project .
```

Native plugins are trusted executables. Schema-3 Docker plugins can run in the isolated mode; use `--require-sandbox` when the policy must reject native plugins.

## Quality commands

```bash
make bootstrap
make test
make coverage-check
make test-race
make lint
make vulncheck
make verify
make verify-strict
```

`make verify` is developer-friendly; generated CI uses strict drift enforcement. The default coverage threshold is `{{.Config.Quality.Coverage.Minimum}}%`. For a brand-new `bare` scaffold with no business-layer statements yet, the coverage gate reports N/A until executable business code exists.

## Architecture

```text
internal/domain          business entities and errors
internal/application     use cases / worker logic
internal/ports           interfaces
internal/infrastructure  delivery, persistence and external adapters
internal/bootstrap       dependency composition and lifecycle
internal/config          runtime configuration
```
